ingot (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The write progress bar counts only data that has reached the device. The
    kernel accepted a whole ISO into the page cache within seconds, so the bar
    hit 100% at once and the real write happened during the final flush with
    no progress shown. The helper now forces data onto the device every
    32 MiB with fdatasync, drops it from the page cache, and reports progress
    from what has been committed. Cancelling also takes effect promptly.
  * Short writes are completed instead of being silently ignored.

 -- Orkun Soylu <103385766+orkun-soylu@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:40:00 +0100

ingot (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed from kalip. The package conflicts with and replaces kalip, so
    installing it removes the old package; downloads cached under the old
    name are carried over.
  * The interface is now in English, with a Turkish translation shipped
    through gettext and chosen from the session language. The build fails
    if a translatable string has no translation.
  * The privileged helper no longer produces interface text. pkexec does not
    pass the session language on, so the helper emits stable status and
    error codes and the interface translates them.
  * Raspberry Pi keyboard layout, time zone and Wi-Fi country default to the
    writing machine's settings instead of fixed Turkish values.

 -- Orkun Soylu <103385766+orkun-soylu@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:30:00 +0100
